+_`<ToggleGroupItem>` gains `#media` and `#meta`, and they are what makes a tile_
+
+An option that holds more than its label says so with its content: a row above the
+label goes in `#media` (a glyph, a thumbnail, a stage), a row below it in `#meta` (a
+readout, a description), and the label stays the default slot. A group in which any item
+fills either slot is a set of tiles: a 16px corner (`--radius-field`) at every size, a
+column, one height per row, a 2px selected edge, a check in the inline-end corner of a
+tile at least 3.5 marks wide, and no plate at rest. Nothing is declared; there is no
+`shape`. A group whose items fill neither slot is pills, as before, and a pill is one
+row (below).
+
+Two call-site patterns change, both where a default slot held two rows:
+
+```vue
+<!-- before: two rows in the default slot, a column and a corner by class -->
+<ToggleGroupItem value="smooth" class="flex-col items-start rounded-pill">
+  <span>Smooth</span>
+  <span>0.5 s · ζ 1</span>
+</ToggleGroupItem>
+<!-- after -->
+<ToggleGroupItem value="smooth">
+  Smooth
+  <template #meta>0.5 s · ζ 1</template>
+</ToggleGroupItem>
+```
+
+Left as it is, that item is now a one-row pill: its two rows run on one line, and a row
+taller than the rung (a 52px stage in a 36px pill) is clipped at the plate. A production
+build says nothing; a development build of your app logs `[ToggleGroupItem] value=…
+asks for a second row …` for an item whose content is clipped, holds a `<br>`, or
+stacks two rows of text inside the rung (a child that sets its own `display: block`).
+Detector: `rg -U '<ToggleGroupItem[^>]*class="[^"]*(flex-col|rounded-)'` (`-U`: the tag
+usually spans lines). Selection paint of your own on an item (`[data-state="on"]` rules
+that set an outline, a border or a stroke) can go: a stroke that reads `currentColor`
+follows the selected ink, and `--selection-tone` on the group or the item tints the
+edge, the plate, the label and that stroke together. Detector:
+`rg '\[data-state="on"\][^{]*(path|svg|outline|border)'`.
+
+_`<FadingScroll>` is a tab stop only when nothing inside it is_
